adjudication.rationale:
In `sendAddGuestsEmails`, the code intentionally sends `AttendeeScheduledEmail` to attendees whose email is in the `newGuests` list, and sends `AttendeeAddGuestsEmail` to all other attendees:
```ts
if (newGuests.includes(attendee.email)) {
  return sendEmail(() => new AttendeeScheduledEmail(calendarEvent, attendee));
} else {
  return sendEmail(() => new AttendeeAddGuestsEmail(calendarEvent, attendee));
}
```
While this matches the finding’s observation, the diff provides no requirement that newly added guests must receive the new “AddGuests” notification template instead of a standard scheduled/confirmation email. Given the naming, it’s plausible (and consistent) that *new* guests should get the full scheduled invite, while existing attendees get an “additional guests added” update. Therefore the finding asserts incorrect behavior without a verifiable defect from the diff alone.
